    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eMushrooms stretch the beef and that is the whole strategy.\u003c/strong\u003e Buy whole white mushrooms rather than pre-sliced, since the sliced packs cost noticeably more per pound for thirty seconds of knife work.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eVelveting is free tenderness.\u003c/strong\u003e Cornstarch and a pinch of baking soda cost essentially nothing and they let you use a cheaper cut without it turning chewy.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eOyster sauce is one bottle that keeps for months.\u003c/strong\u003e It is the backbone of the gravy here and of a lot of other stir fries, so the cost per batch is small once you own it.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eCook the rice ahead so it is not the bottleneck.\u003c/strong\u003e This stir fry cooks in about eight minutes once the pan is hot, and you do not want to be standing there waiting on a rice cooker."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Slice the beef thin against the grain and toss it with most of the cornstarch, a pinch of baking soda, some soy sauce, and a splash of water, then let it sit for at least fifteen minutes.",
                    "Cook the rice according to the package while the beef rests.",
                    "Stir the remaining cornstarch into a little cold water and mix it with the oyster sauce, the rest of the soy sauce, the beef broth, the chicken broth, sugar, salt, and black pepper to make the sauce.",
                    "Heat the vegetable oil in a large skillet or wok until it smokes and sear the beef in batches in a single layer, just until browned, then set it aside. Do not cook it through, since it will finish in the sauce.",
                    "Add the butter to the pan and cook the mushrooms hard, without stirring much, until they release their water, it cooks off, and they brown.",
                    "Add the ginger, garlic, and the white parts of the green onions and cook until fragrant.",
                    "Pour in the sauce mixture, bring it to a boil until it thickens and turns glossy, return the beef, add the sesame oil and the green onion tops, and toss to coat."
                ],
